---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Arithmetic Progressions | CBSE Class 10 Maths | ${provider.name}`}
  description="CBSE Class 10 Maths Chapter 5 notes on Arithmetic Progressions (AP). Master the nth term formula, sum of first n terms, term selection tricks, visual staircase diagrams, and an interactive 20-question board exam quiz."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> / Arithmetic Progressions
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Mathematics · Chapter 5</span>
      <h1>Arithmetic Progressions</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Understand arithmetic sequences, compute any nth term from the beginning or end, derive sum formulas, and solve real-world word problems for the CBSE Class 10 Board Exam.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts &amp; Formulas</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔢 Definition of Arithmetic Progression (AP)</h3>
          <p class="formula">a, a + d, a + 2d, a + 3d, ...</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>An <strong>Arithmetic Progression</strong> is a sequence of numbers in which each term is obtained by adding a fixed number <em>d</em> to the preceding term (except the first term <em>a</em>).</li>
            <li><strong>Common Difference (d):</strong> <code>d = aₙ - aₙ₋₁</code>. Can be <strong>positive, negative, or zero</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Finite vs Infinite AP:</strong> An AP with a last term is finite; otherwise it is infinite.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📌 The n-th Term (General Term) of an AP</h3>
          <p class="formula">aₙ = a + (n - 1)d</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><em>a:</em> First term, &nbsp;<em>d:</em> Common difference, &nbsp;<em>n:</em> Number of terms (always a natural number ℕ).</li>
            <li><strong>n-th term from the end:</strong> If an AP has last term <em>l</em>, the n-th term from the end is:
              <br/><code>aₙ(end) = l - (n - 1)d</code>.
            </li>
            <li>If three numbers <em>a, b, c</em> are in AP, then <code>2b = a + c &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; b = (a + c)/2</code> (where <em>b</em> is called the <strong>Arithmetic Mean</strong>).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>➕ Sum of First n Terms of an AP</h3>
          <p class="formula">Sₙ = n/2 · [2a + (n - 1)d] = n/2 · [a + l]</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>When first term <em>a</em> and common difference <em>d</em> are known: <code>Sₙ = n/2 [2a + (n - 1)d]</code>.</li>
            <li>When first term <em>a</em> and last term <em>l</em> are known: <code>Sₙ = n/2 [a + l]</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Sum of first n natural numbers:</strong> <code>Sₙ = n(n + 1) / 2</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Key recurrence:</strong> <code>aₙ = Sₙ - Sₙ₋₁</code> (for n &gt; 1) and <code>a₁ = S₁</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🎯 Smart Selection of Terms in an AP</h3>
          <p class="formula">Minimizing variables in symmetric problem-solving</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>3 terms in AP:</strong> Let terms be <code>(a - d), a, (a + d)</code> &nbsp;(Common difference = <em>d</em>). Sum equals <code>3a</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>4 terms in AP:</strong> Let terms be <code>(a - 3d), (a - d), (a + d), (a + 3d)</code> &nbsp;(Common difference = <em>2d</em>). Sum equals <code>4a</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>5 terms in AP:</strong> Let terms be <code>(a - 2d), (a - d), a, (a + d), (a + 2d)</code> &nbsp;(Common difference = <em>d</em>). Sum equals <code>5a</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Diagrams Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Visual Concepts: AP Stepping Progression &amp; Term Summation</h2>

      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 1 · The AP Staircase (Constant Common Difference d)</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Arithmetic progression staircase visualization">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- 5 Stairs: a=2, d=3 -> 2, 5, 8, 11, 14 -->
              <!-- Step 1 -->
              <rect x="40" y="180" width="60" height="40" fill="#bae6fd" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="70" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0369a1">a₁ = a</text>

              <!-- Step 2 -->
              <rect x="110" y="150" width="60" height="70" fill="#7dd3fc" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="140" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0369a1">a + d</text>
              <line x1="70" y1="180" x2="140" y2="150" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3"/>
              <text x="105" y="160" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">+d</text>

              <!-- Step 3 -->
              <rect x="180" y="120" width="60" height="100" fill="#38bdf8" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="210" y="175" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">a + 2d</text>
              <line x1="140" y1="150" x2="210" y2="120" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3"/>
              <text x="175" y="130" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">+d</text>

              <!-- Step 4 -->
              <rect x="250" y="90" width="60" height="130" fill="#0284c7" stroke="#0369a1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="280" y="160" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">a + 3d</text>
              <line x1="210" y1="120" x2="280" y2="90" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3"/>
              <text x="245" y="100" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">+d</text>

              <!-- Step 5 (nth term) -->
              <rect x="320" y="60" width="85" height="160" fill="#0369a1" stroke="#075985" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="362" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">aₙ = a+(n-1)d</text>
              <line x1="280" y1="90" x2="362" y2="60" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3"/>
              <text x="320" y="70" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">+d</text>

              <!-- Base Line -->
              <line x1="25" y1="220" x2="430" y2="220" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="230" y="240" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#475569" font-weight="600">Equal increments (d) at every step define an AP.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Each consecutive term rises by constant common difference d: aₙ = a + (n - 1)d.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 2 · Gauss Summation Pairing Formula</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Gauss pairing for AP summation">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- First row of sequence -->
              <g transform="translate(30, 40)">
                <text x="30" y="20" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">Sₙ =</text>
                <text x="80" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">a₁</text>
                <text x="120" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="150" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">a₂</text>
                <text x="190" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="220" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">···</text>
                <text x="250" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="280" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">aₙ₋₁</text>
                <text x="330" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="360" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">aₙ</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Reverse row of sequence -->
              <g transform="translate(30, 85)">
                <text x="30" y="20" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">Sₙ =</text>
                <text x="80" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#ea580c">aₙ</text>
                <text x="120" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="150" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#ea580c">aₙ₋₁</text>
                <text x="190" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="220" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">···</text>
                <text x="250" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="280" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#ea580c">a₂</text>
                <text x="330" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <text x="360" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#ea580c">a₁</text>
              </g>

              <line x1="50" y1="125" x2="420" y2="125" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="2"/>

              <!-- Sum row -->
              <g transform="translate(30, 140)">
                <text x="10" y="20" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">2Sₙ =</text>
                <rect x="65" y="0" width="60" height="28" rx="4" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981"/>
                <text x="95" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">(a + l)</text>
                <text x="135" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+</text>
                <rect x="145" y="0" width="60" height="28" rx="4" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981"/>
                <text x="175" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">(a + l)</text>
                <text x="220" y="20" font-size="13" fill="#64748b">+ ··· +</text>
                <rect x="345" y="0" width="60" height="28" rx="4" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981"/>
                <text x="375" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">(a + l)</text>
              </g>

              <rect x="100" y="190" width="260" height="35" rx="6" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="230" y="212" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2Sₙ = n(a + l) &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; Sₙ = n/2 (a + l)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Gauss inverted summation pairing pairs 1st with last term to prove Sₙ = n/2 [2a + (n - 1)d].</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Solved Step-by-Step Problem -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Exemplar Board Problem: Sum and Terms of an AP Solved</h2>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.75rem; background:var(--paper)">
        <h3 style="color:var(--brand);margin-top:0">Problem: How many terms of the AP 24, 21, 18, ... must be taken so that their sum is 78? Explain the double answer.</h3>
        <div style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text)">
          <p><strong>Step 1 (Identify parameters):</strong> First term <code>a = 24</code>, common difference <code>d = 21 - 24 = -3</code>. Given sum <code>Sₙ = 78</code>.</p>
          <p><strong>Step 2 (Apply sum formula):</strong>
            <br/><code>Sₙ = n/2 [2a + (n - 1)d]</code>
            <br/><code>78 = n/2 [2(24) + (n - 1)(-3)]</code>
            <br/><code>156 = n [48 - 3n + 3] = n [51 - 3n]</code>
            <br/><code>156 = 51n - 3n² &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; 3n² - 51n + 156 = 0</code>
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 3 (Simplify &amp; Factorise):</strong>
            <br/>Divide entire equation by 3:
            <br/><code>n² - 17n + 52 = 0</code>
            <br/>Factors of 52 that add up to -17 are -13 and -4:
            <br/><code>(n - 4)(n - 13) = 0 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; n = 4 &nbsp;or&nbsp; n = 13</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 4 (Explain the double answer):</strong>
            <br/>Both <code>n = 4</code> and <code>n = 13</code> are valid natural numbers.
            <br/>Sum of first 4 terms: <code>24 + 21 + 18 + 15 = 78</code>.
            <br/>The terms from 5th to 13th are: <code>12, 9, 6, 3, 0, -3, -6, -9, -12</code>.
            <br/>Notice the sum of terms from the 5th to the 13th term is <strong>exactly 0</strong> (positive terms cancel negative terms).
            <br/>Therefore, the sum of 4 terms is 78, and adding the subsequent terms still keeps the sum at 78.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Interactive 20-Question Quiz -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Interactive CBSE Board Exam Quiz (20 Questions)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Test your concepts on general terms, sum formulas, nth term from end, and AP applications.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container card" id="quiz-box">
        <div class="quiz-header-bar">
          <span class="quiz-counter" id="quiz-counter">Question 1 of 20</span>
          <span class="quiz-score" id="quiz-score">Score: 0 / 20</span>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-question-body">
          <p class="quiz-q-text" id="quiz-question">Loading question...</p>
          <div class="quiz-options-list" id="quiz-options"></div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="quiz-feedback"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-footer-actions">
          <button class="button secondary" id="quiz-prev-btn" disabled>← Previous</button>
          <button class="button" id="quiz-next-btn" disabled>Next Question →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-completed-banner card" id="quiz-result-box" style="display:none; text-align:center; padding:2.5rem;">
        <h3>Quiz Completed! 🎉</h3>
        <p class="quiz-final-score" id="quiz-final-score" style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--brand); margin:1rem 0;"></p>
        <p id="quiz-final-msg" class="muted"></p>
        <button class="button" id="quiz-restart-btn" style="margin-top:1rem;">Retake Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-banner">
      <h2>Need personalized Maths guidance for Class 10?</h2>
      <p>Book a free {provider.trial.duration_minutes}-minute trial session with {provider.tutor_name} (online or at-home) to master AP formulas, series questions, and board exam word problems.</p>
      <a class="button" href={calBookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book Free Trial</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function() {
  const quizData = [
    {
      q: "In an AP, if d = -4, n = 7, and aₙ = 4, then a is:",
      options: ["6", "7", "20", "28"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "aₙ = a + (n - 1)d ⟹ 4 = a + (7 - 1)(-4) ⟹ 4 = a - 24 ⟹ a = 28."
    },
    {
      q: "The 11th term of the AP -3, -1/2, 2, ... is:",
      options: ["28", "22", "-38", "-46/2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "a = -3. d = -1/2 - (-3) = 5/2. a₁₁ = a + 10d = -3 + 10(5/2) = -3 + 25 = 22."
    },
    {
      q: "Which term of the AP 21, 18, 15, ... is -81?",
      options: ["28th", "34th", "35th", "36th"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "a = 21, d = -3. aₙ = 21 + (n - 1)(-3) = -81 ⟹ -3(n - 1) = -102 ⟹ n - 1 = 34 ⟹ n = 35."
    },
    {
      q: "If the 7th and 13th terms of an AP are 34 and 64 respectively, then its 18th term is:",
      options: ["87", "88", "89", "90"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "a + 6d = 34, a + 12d = 64. Subtracting: 6d = 30 ⟹ d = 5. Then a = 34 - 30 = 4. a₁₈ = a + 17d = 4 + 17(5) = 4 + 85 = 89."
    },
    {
      q: "The sum of the first 16 terms of the AP 10, 6, 2, ... is:",
      options: ["-320", "320", "-352", "-400"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "a = 10, d = -4, n = 16. S₁₆ = 16/2 [2(10) + (16 - 1)(-4)] = 8 [20 - 60] = 8(-40) = -320."
    },
    {
      q: "If the common difference of an AP is 5, then what is a₁₈ - a₁₃?",
      options: ["5", "20", "25", "30"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "a₁₈ - a₁₃ = (a + 17d) - (a + 12d) = 5d = 5(5) = 25."
    },
    {
      q: "The 20th term from the end of the AP 3, 8, 13, ..., 253 is:",
      options: ["148", "153", "158", "163"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "l = 253, d = 5. n-th term from end = l - (n - 1)d = 253 - (20 - 1)(5) = 253 - 19(5) = 253 - 95 = 158."
    },
    {
      q: "The sum of first n odd natural numbers is:",
      options: ["2n - 1", "2n + 1", "n²", "n² - 1"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Sequence: 1, 3, 5, ... with a = 1, d = 2. Sₙ = n/2 [2(1) + (n - 1)2] = n/2 [2 + 2n - 2] = n/2 (2n) = n²."
    },
    {
      q: "If 2x, x + 10, 3x + 2 are in AP, then the value of x is:",
      options: ["0", "2", "4", "6"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "For terms in AP: 2(b) = a + c ⟹ 2(x + 10) = 2x + (3x + 2) ⟹ 2x + 20 = 5x + 2 ⟹ 3x = 18 ⟹ x = 6."
    },
    {
      q: "If the sum of first n terms of an AP is Sₙ = 3n² + 5n, then its common difference d is:",
      options: ["3", "5", "6", "8"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "For Sₙ = An² + Bn, common difference is always 2A. Here A = 3, so d = 2(3) = 6. Alternatively: S₁ = 8 = a₁. S₂ = 3(4) + 10 = 22. a₂ = S₂ - S₁ = 22 - 8 = 14. d = a₂ - a₁ = 14 - 8 = 6."
    },
    {
      q: "How many two-digit numbers are divisible by 3?",
      options: ["25", "30", "32", "33"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Two digit numbers divisible by 3: 12, 15, ..., 99. Here a = 12, d = 3, aₙ = 99. 99 = 12 + (n - 1)3 ⟹ 87 = 3(n - 1) ⟹ n - 1 = 29 ⟹ n = 30."
    },
    {
      q: "The first and last terms of an AP are 1 and 11. If the sum of its terms is 36, then the number of terms is:",
      options: ["5", "6", "7", "8"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Sₙ = n/2 (a + l) ⟹ 36 = n/2 (1 + 11) ⟹ 36 = n/2 (12) ⟹ 36 = 6n ⟹ n = 6."
    },
    {
      q: "In an AP, if a = 3.5, d = 0, n = 101, then aₙ will be:",
      options: ["0", "3.5", "103.5", "104.5"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "When common difference d = 0, every term is equal to the first term. Hence a₁₀₁ = 3.5."
    },
    {
      q: "If the nth term of an AP is (2n + 1), then the sum of its first n terms is:",
      options: ["n(n + 2)", "n(n + 1)", "n²", "n(n - 1)"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "a₁ = 2(1) + 1 = 3. Last term l = 2n + 1. Sₙ = n/2 [a + l] = n/2 [3 + 2n + 1] = n/2 [2n + 4] = n(n + 2)."
    },
    {
      q: "Which term of the AP 121, 117, 113, ... is its first negative term?",
      options: ["30th", "31st", "32nd", "33rd"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "a = 121, d = -4. aₙ < 0 ⟹ 121 + (n - 1)(-4) < 0 ⟹ 125 - 4n < 0 ⟹ 4n > 125 ⟹ n > 31.25. The least integer is n = 32."
    },
    {
      q: "Find the sum of all odd integers between 2 and 100 divisible by 3:",
      options: ["867", "834", "800", "900"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Numbers are 3, 9, 15, ..., 99. Here a = 3, d = 6, l = 99. 99 = 3 + (n - 1)6 ⟹ 96 = 6(n - 1) ⟹ n - 1 = 16 ⟹ n = 17. S₁₇ = 17/2 (3 + 99) = 17/2 (102) = 17 × 51 = 867."
    },
    {
      q: "If 7 times the 7th term of an AP is equal to 11 times its 11th term, then its 18th term will be:",
      options: ["7", "11", "18", "0"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "7 · a₇ = 11 · a₁₁ ⟹ 7(a + 6d) = 11(a + 10d) ⟹ 7a + 42d = 11a + 110d ⟹ 4a + 68d = 0 ⟹ 4(a + 17d) = 0 ⟹ a + 17d = 0 ⟹ a₁₈ = 0."
    },
    {
      q: "If the sum of 3 numbers in AP is 24 and their product is 440, the numbers are:",
      options: ["5, 8, 11", "4, 8, 12", "6, 8, 10", "3, 8, 13"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Let numbers be a - d, a, a + d. Sum = 3a = 24 ⟹ a = 8. Product = (8 - d)(8)(8 + d) = 440 ⟹ 8(64 - d²) = 440 ⟹ 64 - d² = 55 ⟹ d² = 9 ⟹ d = ±3. Numbers are 5, 8, 11."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the common difference of an AP in which a₂₁ - a₇ = 84?",
      options: ["4", "5", "6", "7"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "a₂₁ - a₇ = (a + 20d) - (a + 6d) = 14d. Given 14d = 84 ⟹ d = 84 / 14 = 6."
    },
    {
      q: "The angles of a quadrilateral are in AP whose common difference is 10°. The smallest angle is:",
      options: ["65°", "75°", "80°", "85°"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Let angles be a, a + 10, a + 20, a + 30. Sum of angles of quadrilateral = 360°. 4a + 60 = 360 ⟹ 4a = 300 ⟹ a = 75°."
    }
  ];

  let currentIdx = 0;
  let userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);

  const qText = document.getElementById("quiz-question");
  const optionsBox = document.getElementById("quiz-options");
  const feedbackBox = document.getElementById("quiz-feedback");
  const counterBox = document.getElementById("quiz-counter");
  const scoreBox = document.getElementById("quiz-score");
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-prev-btn");
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-next-btn");
  const quizBox = document.getElementById("quiz-box");
  const resultBox = document.getElementById("quiz-result-box");
  const finalScore = document.getElementById("quiz-final-score");
  const finalMsg = document.getElementById("quiz-final-msg");
  const restartBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-restart-btn");

  function renderQuestion(idx) {
    const item = quizData[idx];
    counterBox.textContent = `Question ${idx + 1} of ${quizData.length}`;
    qText.textContent = item.q;
    optionsBox.innerHTML = "";
    feedbackBox.textContent = "";
    feedbackBox.className = "quiz-feedback";

    const selected = userAnswers[idx];

    item.options.forEach((optText, oIdx) => {
      const btn = document.createElement("button");
      btn.className = "quiz-opt-btn";
      btn.textContent = `${String.fromCharCode(65 + oIdx)}. ${optText}`;

      if (selected !== null) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        if (oIdx === item.answer) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-correct");
        } else if (oIdx === selected) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-wrong");
        }
      } else {
        btn.onclick = () => selectOption(oIdx);
      }

      optionsBox.appendChild(btn);
    });

    if (selected !== null) {
      if (selected === item.answer) {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✓ Correct! ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-correct");
      } else {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✗ Incorrect. Correct answer is option ${String.fromCharCode(65 + item.answer)}. ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-wrong");
      }
    }

    prevBtn.disabled = idx === 0;
    nextBtn.disabled = selected === null;
    nextBtn.textContent = idx === quizData.length - 1 ? "Finish Quiz →" : "Next Question →";
    updateScoreDisplay();
  }

  function selectOption(oIdx) {
    userAnswers[currentIdx] = oIdx;
    renderQuestion(currentIdx);
  }

  function updateScoreDisplay() {
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    scoreBox.textContent = `Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length}`;
  }

  prevBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx > 0) {
      currentIdx--;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    }
  };

  nextBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
      currentIdx++;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    } else {
      finishQuiz();
    }
  };

  function finishQuiz() {
    quizBox.style.display = "none";
    resultBox.style.display = "block";
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    finalScore.textContent = `Your Final Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length} (${Math.round((score / quizData.length) * 100)}%)`;
    if (score >= 18) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Superb mastery! You have completely mastered Arithmetic Progressions and term summations.";
    } else if (score >= 14) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Well done! Review the double answer summation explanation and term selection to achieve 100%.";
    } else {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Keep practicing! Review the formulas and exemplar problem above, then retry.";
    }
  }

  restartBtn.onclick = () => {
    userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);
    currentIdx = 0;
    resultBox.style.display = "none";
    quizBox.style.display = "block";
    renderQuestion(0);
  };

  renderQuestion(0);
})();
</script>

